    kg:textSpan "of the decoder. However, in an utterance there may be repeated phonemes that have very similar annotations, which consequently result in matching to all similarly sounding locations, as shown in Fig. 2 (b). The gating procedure prevents this behavior by conning the search to locations that are near the inputs relevant to the previously generated symbol. It is, however, important to notice that the shape of the gating function d is not dened a priori, but learned. In Fig. 3, we show the shape of " .

