    kg:docId "1602.02410_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/1602_02410_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "is no longer explicitly parametrized by the vocabulary size or the language. This has shown to help when using byte-level input embeddings for named entity recognition ( Gillick et al. , 2015 ), 4.2. Model Setup and we hope it will enable similar gains when used to map onto words. The typical measure used for reporting progress in language modeling is perplexity, which is the average per-word log-probability on the holdout data set: e 1 3.3. Char LSTM Predictions N P i ln p wi . We follow the st" .

