    kg:textSpan "overcondence was problem proposed for the Inception image recognition architecture [ 16 ]. For the purpose of computing the training cost the ground-truth label distribution is smoothed, with some fraction of the probability mass assigned to classes other than the correct one. This in turn prevents the model from learning to concentrate all probability mass on a single token. Additionally, the model receives more training signal because the error function cannot easily saturate. Originally unifo" .

