<http://example.org/kg/chunk/1702_07793_rag__chunk_001> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "1702.07793_rag::chunk_001" ;
    kg:docId "1702.07793_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/1702_07793_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "practice. Traditional acoustic model training is based on frame-wise cross entropy loss (CE), which requires pre-generated and aligned frame labels by hidden Markov model/Gaussian mixture model (HMM/GMM) paradigm. To simplify this process, Graves et al. ( 2006 ) introduced CTC objective function to infer speech-label alignments automatically without any intermediate process, leading to an end-to-end system for ASR. CTC technique has shown promising results in Deep Speech ( Hannun et al. , 2014 ;" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/1702_07793_rag__chunk_011> a kg:Chunk ;
