    kg:docId "1705.08947_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/1705_08947_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "voiced. Hidden states are also used to make two separate normalized F 0 predictions. The rst prediction, f GRU , is made with a single-layer bidirectional GRU followed by an afne projection. The second prediction, f conv , is made by adding up the contributions of multiple convolutions with varying convolution widths and a single output channel. Finally, the hidden state is used with an afne projection and a sigmoid nonlinearity to predict a mixture ratio , which is used to weigh the two normali" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/1705_08947_rag__chunk_005> a kg:Chunk ;
