    kg:textSpan "to extract 60-dimensional Mel-Cepstral Coefcients (MCCs), 1- dimensional band aperiodicities (BAP) and F 0 in log-scale in 5-ms step. So the nal acoustic features were 63-dimensions including one extra binary voiced/unvoiced ag. As for the text, we made a complex text analysis module to get 138- dimensional linguistic features, including phoneme information, prosody boundary labeling, part of speech tagging, state information and corresponding position index. To benchmark the performance of the " .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/1707_01670_rag__chunk_008> a kg:Chunk ;
