    kg:textSpan "processing approaches Different signal processing approaches have been explored to nd some convenient low-resolution audio representations that can both be easily modelled and efciently converted back to temporal audio. For example, the Grifn-Lim (Grifn & Lim, 1984) algorithm allows one to efciently decode an STFT sequence back to the temporal signal at the cost of introducing strong, robotic artifacts as noted in Wang et al. (2017). More sophisticated representations and signal processing techn" .

