    kg:textSpan "BiRNN [17] and BiLatRNN [18] for condence prediction. small. Once lattice arcs have been aligned with CN arcs a number of approaches, such as simple averaging or an attention mechanism, can be used to yield lattice features for CN arcs. Table 2 shows that the use of sub-word information (embedding, +duration) and more complex representations (+encoder) yields small but consistent gains. The BiRNN examined so far lacked any information about competing transcriptions available within CNs. Dependin" .

