    kg:textSpan "autoencoder (VAE) based models have gained popularity in non-parallel voice conversion recently. However, they often suffer from difcult training process and unsatisfactory results. In this paper, we propose CVC, a contrastive learning-based adversarial approach for voice conversion. Compared to previous CycleGAN-based methods, CVC only requires an efcient one-way GAN training by taking the advantage of contrastive learning. When it comes to nonparallel one-to-one voice conversion, CVC is on par" .

