    kg:docId "2104.12870_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2104_12870_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "utterance condence does not take advantage of word-level training signals. This paper proposes to jointly learn word con- dence, word deletion, and utterance condence. Empirical results show that multi-task learning with all three objectives improves condence metrics (NCE, AUC, RMSE) without the need for increasing the model size of the condence estimation module. Using the utterance-level condence for rescoring also decreases the word error rates on Googles Voice Search and Long-tail Maps datas" .

