    kg:textSpan "mel-spectrograms than Grad-TTS we propose. We believe this is because the task of reconstructing mel-spectrogram from pure noise N (0 , I ) is more difcult than the one of reconstructing it from its noisy copy N ( , I ) . One possible objection could be that the model trained with N (0 , I ) as terminal distribution can just add to this noise at the rst step of sampling (it is possible because s has as its input) and then repeat the same steps as our model to generate data from N ( , I ) . In th" .

