    kg:textSpan "ON PROSODY MODELING FOR ASR+TTS BASED VOICE CONVERSION Wen-Chin Huang 1 , Tomoki Hayashi 1 , Xinjian Li 2 , Shinji Watanabe 2 , Tomoki Toda 1 1 Nagoya University, Japan 2 Carnegie Mellon University, USA ABSTRACT In voice conversion (VC), an approach showing promising results in the latest voice conversion challenge (VCC) 2020 is to rst use an automatic speech recognition (ASR) model to transcribe the source speech into the underlying linguistic contents; these are then used as input by a text-to" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2107_09477_rag__chunk_002> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2107.09477_rag::chunk_002" ;
    kg:docId "2107.09477_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2107_09477_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "to as target text prediction (TTP) . We borrow the idea from [14] and train a text prediction (TP) module to generate the prosody embedding from the text derived from the source speech. Figure 1b illustrates this process. The TP module is rst pretrained with a GST-TTS on a multispeaker dataset, and further ne-tuned in a target-speaker-dependent manner. As a result, TTP does not suffer from a mismatch between training and conversion unlike SPT. Our contributions in this work are as follows. 2.2. " .

