    kg:textSpan "of a series of selfattention layers [1]. Each layer relies on calculating a distance between each pair of items from the input sequence. Although this allows each input item to attend to any other item in the sequence, this results in a complexity of O ( n 2 ) with respect to the input sequence length n , in terms of both memory and computation effort. Reducing the quadratic complexity has been the target of several approaches in natural language processing, the idea being to restrict each input" .

