    kg:textSpan "and speed) by a natural language sentence. To realize this target, we turn to cross-modal representation learning. The details will be discussed later. C. Expressive Text-to-speech In the field of expressive speech synthesis, several works [6], [9], [12], [27][30] have been done. Wang et al. [6] propose to use global style tokens to control and transfer global speaking styles. Inspired by [6], many similar works propose to learn speaking style from a reference audio, such as, Li et al. [27] use " .

