    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/1912_02522_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "of the current state of technology through public evaluation tools; and (iii) provide an open-source free dataset accessible to all. While speech technologies have developed rapidly during the last few decades (with a large focus on speaker verication), speaker recognition under noisy and unconstrained conditions is still an extremely challenging topic. Applications of speaker recognition are many and varied, ranging from authentication in high-security systems and forensic tests, to high delity" .

