    kg:textSpan "Voice Conversion Can Improve ASR in Very Low-Resource Settings Matthew Baas and Herman Kamper MediaLab, E&E Engineering, Stellenbosch University, South Africa 20786379@sun.ac.za, kamperh@sun.ac.za Abstract Voice conversion (VC) could be used to improve speech recognition systems in low-resource languages by using it to augment limited training data. However, VC has not been widely used for this purpose because of practical issues such as compute speed and limitations when converting to and from " .

