    kg:textSpan "pretrained features to transformations is crucial to downstream tasks. Recent works have proposed methods to encourage invariance for vision tasks. However, for audio applications, learning invariant representations without using labeled data remains a challenge. Inspired by recent advances in SSL for audio, we propose an augmented contrastive learning framework that learns invariant features using unlabeled data. In this approach, the embeddings are learnt by comparing multiple augmented audio " .

