    kg:textSpan "a single network. In this work we present a single sequence-to-sequence ASR model trained on 9 different Indian languages, which have very little overlap in their scripts. Specically, we take a union of language-specic grapheme sets and train a grapheme-based sequence-to-sequence model jointly on data from all languages. We nd that this model, which is not explicitly given any information about language identity, improves recognition performance by 21% relative compared to analogous sequence-to-" .

