    kg:textSpan "or joint front- and back-end techniques (as shown in Fig. 1). We highlight the advantages and disadvantages of the different approaches and paradigms, and establish interrelations and differences among the prominent techniques. This overview assumes that the readers have background knowledge in noise-robust ASR and deep learning. However, we provide some key concepts of the raised noise-robust speech recognition problem and neural networks, e. g., fully-connected layers, convolutional layers, an" .

