<http://example.org/kg/chunk/1910_11933_rag__chunk_001> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "1910.11933_rag::chunk_001" ;
    kg:docId "1910.11933_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/1910_11933_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "are typically available. This paper examines this limited resource scenario for condence estimation, a measure commonly used to assess transcription reliability. In particular, it explores what other sources of word and sub-word level information available in the transcription process could be used to improve condence scores. To encode all such information this paper extends lattice recurrent neural networks to handle sub-words. Experimental results using the IARPA OpenKWS 2016 evaluation system" .

